# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 13 of the Tutorial

[AS7's Example 19.1 (z parameters)]

r1,1,2,20
r2,2,0,40
r3,2,3,30

analysis: dc
note: In this problem, we find a two-port equivalent for the first time. Determine the z parameters of the T network between nodes 1 and 3: z11 = 60, z12 = z21 = 40, z22 = 70.
tool: port
n1: 1
n2: 3
kind: z
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[AS7's Example 19.2 (a two-port as an element)]

e,1,0,100
z,1,2,[40,20j,30j,50]
r,2,0,10

analysis: ac
note: In this problem, we use a two-port as an element for the first time, with its four parameters riding in the description's fourth term (z,1,2,[40,20j,30j,50] — the order is 11, 12, 21, 22). Find I1 and I2 — aa(iz1) and aa(iz2).
omega: omega
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: yes


